Create a new workflow definition in a specified Project.

USAGE:
  scw workflows definition create [arg=value ...]

ARGS:
  name=<generated>                      Name of the workflow definition
  [description]                         Description of the workflow
  [project-id]                          Project ID to use. If none is passed the default project ID will be used
  [environment-variables.{key}]         Environment variables of the workflow
  [workflow-timeout]                    Timeout of the workflow in seconds
  [cron-schedule.schedule]              
  [cron-schedule.timezone-identifier]   
  [cron-schedule.overlap]                (unknown_schedule_overlap_policy | forbid | buffer_one | buffer_all | allow_all)
  [workflow-version.name]               
  [workflow-version.description]        
  [workflow-version.workflow-dsl]       
  [region=fr-par]                       Region to target. If none is passed will use default region from the config (fr-par)

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for create
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use
